TITLE:: PianoRollPattern
SUMMARY:: Expands a viewable pattern into piano-roll notes.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/ViewablePattern, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/Pbind, Classes/Ppar, Classes/WriteCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollPattern:: turns a pattern LINK::Classes/ViewablePattern:: has already accepted into notes. LINK::#*from:: returns CODE::nil:: unless LINK::Classes/ViewablePattern#*isViewablePattern:: is true. It does not decide those rules.

Per LINK::Classes/Pbind::, every key is expanded to that event count, then the steps are walked on that part's own clock. Step length is CODE::dur * stretch::, defaulting to CODE::1 * 1::. The pattern duration is the sum of those step lengths, including the final note or chord. Note length is CODE::legato * step::, default legato CODE::0.8::, so a note can end before or after that final step. A rest advances time and emits no note. Times stay relative to 0. The roll adds its margin when it places them.

Pitch is a numeric CODE::\midinote:: when present, including chord arrays. Otherwise a default LINK::Classes/Event:: resolves CODE::\note:: or CODE::\degree:: (default midinote 60). The note number is rounded and clipped to 0–127. Amplitude defaults to CODE::0.5:: when CODE::\amp:: is absent. Velocity is that amplitude mapped with CODE::linlin(0, 1, 0, 127):: and rounded. Other keys are copied onto the note, split across a chord when the value is an array of the same size. CODE::\dur::, CODE::\stretch::, CODE::\legato::, CODE::\amp::, CODE::\midinote::, and CODE::\part:: are applied as timing, pitch, and part rather than copied as extra keys.

A lone CODE::Pbind:: is part 1. Each CODE::Ppar:: child is part 1, 2, and so on in list order. An integer CODE::\part:: overrides that. For a CODE::Ppar::, the duration is the longer child, each child including its own final CODE::\dur::. The CODE::Ppar:: repeats value is not written. Finite CODE::Pseq:: repeats are that stream's length. A longer stream is cut to the shorter one.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: from
Expands CODE::pattern:: when it is viewable.

ARGUMENT:: pattern
A LINK::Classes/Pattern::.

RETURNS::
A TELETYPE::PianoRollPattern::, or CODE::nil:: when the pattern is not viewable.

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollPattern:: from a duration and note events. LINK::#*from:: is the usual constructor.

ARGUMENT:: duration
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::. The sum of the step lengths, including the final step.

ARGUMENT:: notes
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Event::s. Each event has CODE::startTime::, CODE::stopTime::, CODE::noteNumber::, CODE::velocity::, CODE::partNumber::, CODE::amp::, CODE::legato::, and CODE::eventKeys::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: duration
The phrase length in beats, including the final step's CODE::\dur::. This is not the last note's stop time.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::.

METHOD:: notes
One event per note. Times are relative to 0.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Event::s.

PRIVATE:: init, prBuild, prChordValue, prEmit, prFiniteLength, prNotesForPbind, prPitches, prStepIsRest, prStreams, prValueAt
